    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="0719" n="707" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg707"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/2528<hi rendition="#superscript"
                    >4/8</hi></note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of the
                        American Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Duggan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-12">July 12, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>: I called Francis White<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d844-f1"/> and informed him that I had been instructed to request
                    the Council to be kind enough to advise the Department of its attitude with
                    regard to the formula for settling the Colombian debt discussed in your office
                    on Saturday, July 6th. I urged Mr. White to get in touch with the members of his
                    Executive Committee as rapidly as possible, in view of the fact that the powers
                    of the President of Colombia to settle the debt expire on July 20.</p>
                <p>Mr. White stated that the matter was so important that he would require for
                    presentation a written letter of what the offer comprised. Although I indicated
                    that Mr. Traphagen knew as well as we did what the agreement arrived at was, I
                    would see that he had a letter in his hands tomorrow morning.</p>
                <p>I asked Mr. White how soon he felt that he would be able to convene his
                    Committee. At first he said Tuesday, but later said he would endeavor to convene
                    it on Monday,<anchor n="14" xml:id="d844-f2"/> if he could.</p>
                <p>I am having a letter prepared for your signature.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d844-f3"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurence Duggan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
